WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.840
A clinic’s day includes much more than the consultation: bookings, waiting patients, reports, payments and questions after the visit.

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:09.903
Sahayak brings those activities together.

00:00:09.903 --> 00:00:18.980
Let us look at the screens that help the whole clinic team keep the day organised and spend less time chasing updates.

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:23.130
Choose the everyday help your clinic needs.

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:27.765
Assistants can support patient entry, clinic questions, intake and follow-up tasks.

00:00:27.765 --> 00:00:34.929
The clinic can turn supported tasks on or pause them, and decide which doctors can use them.

00:00:34.929 --> 00:00:38.300
The help fits the way the clinic works.

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:43.073
Consider a patient who cannot call during working hours.

00:00:43.073 --> 00:00:48.235
A text conversation lets them ask about the clinic and request an appointment.

00:00:48.235 --> 00:00:56.970
The assistant uses the clinic’s information and booking flow, reducing routine interruptions while making it easier for the patient to reach you.

00:00:58.170 --> 00:01:01.827
The arrival page brings check-in and consultation payment settings together.

00:01:01.827 --> 00:01:08.774
A patient’s arrival can connect to the booking and queue, while the payment record stays attached to the visit.

00:01:08.774 --> 00:01:14.990
Reception and the care team get a clearer picture of who has arrived and who is ready.

00:01:16.190 --> 00:01:21.458
Here is the clinic’s day: appointments, the waiting queue and items needing attention.

00:01:21.458 --> 00:01:26.726
If the doctor is delayed, an authorised team member can review revised times.

00:01:26.726 --> 00:01:33.210
One clear view helps the team coordinate the day without repeatedly asking each other for updates.

00:01:34.410 --> 00:01:35.238
Someone cancels.

00:01:35.238 --> 00:01:43.513
The waiting list gives that opening a next step: offer it to an eligible patient who wants an earlier appointment.

00:01:43.513 --> 00:01:48.478
Offers expire, and acceptance is checked before the replacement booking is saved.

00:01:48.478 --> 00:01:53.030
This helps the clinic make better use of available consultation time.

00:01:54.230 --> 00:01:58.775
A test has been requested, but has the report come back?

00:01:58.775 --> 00:02:00.841
Has the doctor reviewed it?

00:02:00.841 --> 00:02:02.907
Has the patient been informed?

00:02:02.907 --> 00:02:04.972
These stages are visible here.

00:02:04.972 --> 00:02:11.170
The care team can spot unfinished follow-up and track responsibility instead of relying on memory.

00:02:12.370 --> 00:02:16.695
Patients do not always explain their concerns in the consultation.

00:02:16.695 --> 00:02:19.722
A post-visit question gives them another opportunity.

00:02:19.722 --> 00:02:29.670
Responses come back to this screen, where the care team can see what needs attention, arrange follow-up and identify recurring suggestions for improvement.

00:02:30.870 --> 00:02:35.184
The inbox brings patient questions and concerns into one place.

00:02:35.184 --> 00:02:41.223
When a conversation needs personal attention, the context is available for a human handoff.

00:02:41.223 --> 00:02:49.850
The clinic team can handle routine requests and direct clinical questions to the doctor, with less searching through separate conversations.

00:02:51.050 --> 00:02:55.827
A solo doctor can manage the clinic and care from one workspace.

00:02:55.827 --> 00:03:00.603
A larger clinic can divide access between the owner, doctors and reception.

00:03:00.603 --> 00:03:07.370
Each person gets the work relevant to their role, so responsibility is shared across the clinic team.

00:03:08.570 --> 00:03:13.692
Connected services help the clinic bring supported outside systems into its workflow.

00:03:13.692 --> 00:03:17.534
The clinic administrator can review the connection status here.

00:03:17.534 --> 00:03:24.790
The benefit is a connected visit with less repeated entry as services are linked to the clinic.

00:03:25.990 --> 00:03:28.657
This screen controls patient check-in messages.

00:03:28.657 --> 00:03:32.658
The clinic administrator chooses the invitation and timing once.

00:03:32.658 --> 00:03:38.882
When a visit finishes, Sahayak schedules the message with the patient’s private feedback link.

00:03:38.882 --> 00:03:46.440
The team follows the delivery status, and the patient’s response returns to the feedback screen for action.

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:54.086
The clinic owner and authorised team members can review clinic activity, recorded collections and outstanding amounts.

00:03:54.086 --> 00:04:02.950
This makes it easier to see what has been recorded and what needs attention, without piecing together the day from separate lists.

00:04:04.150 --> 00:04:14.026
The feature directory brings the clinic’s tools together: patient records, dictation, doctor-selected prescriptions, certificates, care plans and paperwork tracking.

00:04:14.026 --> 00:04:22.342
Team members use the tools available to their role, while doctors review and approve clinical content.

00:04:22.342 --> 00:04:27.020
Information already captured can be reused, reducing repetitive work.

00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:31.288
The value is in a connected day.

00:04:31.288 --> 00:04:33.917
Patients can begin with a message.

00:04:33.917 --> 00:04:41.806
The clinic team manages arrivals, the queue and follow-up, while the doctor focuses on consultations and clinical decisions.

00:04:41.806 --> 00:04:48.380
Sahayak connects their work, so everyone can contribute to a clearer, more organised patient experience.
